0:{"buildId":"","data":[{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"min-h-screen ","style":{"backgroundColor":"hsl(var(--content-bg))"},"children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"3e181358e45b6bbedd4f.htc\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Strategy\",\"item\":\"243c02504f27963696d8.htc\"}]}"}}],["$","nav",null,{"aria-label":"Breadcrumb","className":"max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 pt-6","children":["$","ol",null,{"className":"flex items-center space-x-2 text-sm","style":{"color":"hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))"},"children":[["$","li","/",{"className":"flex items-center","children":[false,["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/","className":"transition-colors hover:opacity-80","style":{"color":"hsl(var(--content-fg))"},"children":"Home"}]]}],["$","li","1eb72b087b11889a850b.htc",{"className":"flex items-center","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mx-2","children":"/"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"font-medium","style":{"color":"hsl(var(--content-fg))"},"children":"Strategy"}]]}]]}]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-8","children":[["$","h1",null,{"className":"text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-8","style":{"color":"hsl(var(--content-fg))"},"children":"Klondike Solitaire Strategy - Tips to Win"}],"$undefined","$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"prose prose-lg max-w-none","children":[["$","section","0",{"className":"mb-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold mb-4","style":{"color":"hsl(var(--content-fg))"},"children":"Prioritize Face-Down Cards"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"whitespace-pre-line leading-relaxed","style":{"color":"hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))"},"children":"The most important strategy in Klondike is to uncover face-down cards as quickly as possible. Every face-down card you flip reveals new information and opens new possibilities.\n\nWhen choosing between two valid moves, always prefer the one that uncovers a face-down card. Moving a card from a column with 4 face-down cards is almost always better than moving a card from a column with 1 face-down card.\n\nFocus on the longest columns first. Column 7 has 6 face-down cards, while column 2 has only 1. Uncovering cards in longer columns provides the most benefit because each flip potentially unlocks a chain of further moves.\n\nThink of face-down cards as locked resources. Each one you flip is like opening a treasure chest â€” it might contain exactly the card you need to progress. The sooner you unlock them, the more options you have for the rest of the game."}]]}],["$","section","1",{"className":"mb-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold mb-4","style":{"color":"hsl(var(--content-fg))"},"children":"Don't Rush to Foundations"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"whitespace-pre-line leading-relaxed","style":{"color":"hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))"},"children":"A common beginner mistake is moving cards to the foundations as soon as possible. While building foundations is the goal, keeping certain cards on the tableau can be more strategically useful.\n\nConsider this: if you move the 5 of hearts to the foundation, it can no longer be used as a building target on the tableau. If you later need to place a black 4 somewhere, you have lost one potential destination.\n\nGeneral guidelines for foundation play:\n\nAlways move Aces immediately â€” they have no tableau value.\nAlways move 2s immediately â€” they can only hold Aces, which go to foundations anyway.\nMove 3s and above only when you are confident they will not be needed for tableau building.\nKeep your foundation piles roughly balanced â€” if one suit is far ahead, you may be locking yourself out of useful moves.\n\nThe exception is the endgame. Once all face-down cards are revealed, move everything to foundations as fast as possible â€” there is no longer any reason to hold cards back."}]]}],"$L3","$L4","$L5","$L6"]}],"$L7","$L8"]}],"$L9"]}],null,"$La"]}],"isPartial":"$@b","staleTime":"$c","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$Ld","isPartial":"$@e","staleTime":"$c","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$Lf","isPartial":"$@10","staleTime":"$c","varyParams":"$11"}],"isUpgradeableISRFallback":false,"a":"$@12","rootVaryParams":null,"needsRuntimeRequest":"$@13"}
